mode: "100644"
text: "# The REACT framework — participation people actually want to give\n\nInteractive content converts scrollers into participants — but only when the ask is worth a tap and the loop gets\nclosed. Each letter is a gate; most interactive content fails at A (a generic ask) or C (no follow-through).\n\n## R — Reason to participate\nEvery ask does a **job for the audience**, not just for your metrics: involve them in a **real decision** (\"which\ncover — A or B?\" makes followers feel ownership), name a **relatable struggle** (\"do you also…?\"), open a\n**genuine opinion split** (a this-or-that people actually debate), or offer a **payoff for playing** (a quiz\nwhere the answer teaches something). If the only beneficiary is your engagement graph, it's filler — and filler\ngets ignored.\n\n## E — Effortless first tap\nMatch the friction to the ask. The ladder: **poll tap** (one touch) → **slider** (nuance without typing) →\n**quiz** (a game) → **question box** (typing) → **comment/UGC** (highest effort). Open with the lowest-friction\nask and escalate: a poll (\"have you tried X? yes/no\") followed by a question box (\"if yes — what happened?\") is a\nclassic stack that converts tap-participants into storytellers. Low-friction taps are also **high-value\nalgorithmic signals** — participation compounds reach.\n\n## A — Ask something specific\nVague stalls, specific converts. **Scope the AMA** (\"ask me anything about [topic]\" — never a bare AMA); make the\npoll concrete (\"which of these two covers?\" not \"thoughts?\"); make quiz questions have a **teaching payoff**\n(wrong answers are fun/myth-busting, never punishing); make every option meaningfully different. Every question is\ntrue — no fabricated quiz \"facts,\" no rigged options.\n\n## C — Close the loop\nThe follow-through is where the value lives: **share the results back** (\"78% of you said…\"), **answer publicly**\n(with permission — visible answers are the social proof that pulls more in), and **batch 5–10 answers into a\nseries** — one question box feeds days of content. Reply to participants (route to `reply-and-comment-writer`;\nthe human sends). An unclosed loop teaches the audience that participating does nothing.\n\n## T — Turn responses into content + insight\nEvery interaction is a **micro-survey**: poll splits become follow-up content (\"you asked for X — here it is\"),\nstruggles become the content calendar, quiz misses reveal what to teach next. Feed findings into\n`audience-research` and the pipeline — honestly framed (a self-selected Story poll is direction, not a study;\nreal research routes to `data-and-original-research`). The **human reads the native results** and adds the native\nstickers in-app; the agent designs, drafts, and turns the real responses into the next round; **WoopSocial\npublishes** the feed-post versions.\n"
